```python
def is_palindrome(s):
    length = len(s)

    for i in range(length // 2):
        if s[i] != s[length - i - 1]:
            return False
    return True
```

This function iterates through only half of the string (which reduces unnecessary comparisons), and directly returns `False` when it finds any mismatch, ensuring fast termination.
